        70.86609649658203,
        67.39069366455078,
        527.3970336914062,
        81.83369445800781
      ],
      "text": "bedaquiline (89% versus 97%, p=0.9). Residual confounding (including confounding by indication)",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        80.59070587158203,
        181.3375244140625,
        95.03370666503906
      ],
      "text": "was thought to be likely.",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        102.29462432861328,
        527.11865234375,
        116.73762512207031
      ],
      "text": "A child-friendly formulation of bedaquiline (20 mg scored uncoated tablet) is being used in the Janssen",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 10.955961227416992,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        115.49463653564453,
        527.4135131835938,
        129.93763732910156
      ],
      "text": "C211 study to dose children aged below 5 years and will also soon be used in an updated protocol",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        128.69459533691406,
        527.4266357421875,
        143.13758850097656
      ],
      "text": "of IMPAACT study P1108 (this study has used the 100 mg formulation to date in all age groups). No",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        141.8946075439453,
        527.3981323242188,
        156.3376007080078
      ],
      "text": "head-to-head studies were conducted to examine the bioequivalence of the 20 mg and the 100 mg",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        155.09474182128906,
        527.4156494140625,
        169.53773498535156
      ],
      "text": "formulation of bedaquiline. Indirect bioequivalence testing showed that both tablets have the same",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        168.29469299316406,
        527.295654296875,
        182.73768615722656
      ],
      "text": "bioavailability and can be used interchangeably at the same total dose. Findings from the bedaquiline",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 10.980732917785645,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        178.70069885253906,
        527.4406127929688,
        195.9376983642578
      ],
      "text": "(85) crush study   also showed that bioavailability of bedaquiline tablets suspended in water was the",
      "font": "SegoeUI-LightItalic",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        194.69471740722656,
        239.72711181640625,
        209.13771057128906
      ],
      "text": "same as for tablets swallowed whole.",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        216.22262573242188,
        527.4140625,
        230.8416290283203
      ],
      "text": "GDG considerations:  The GDG discussed the desirable effects that were previously reported and",
      "font": "SegoeUI-SemiboldItalic",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        229.59864807128906,
        527.3020629882812,
        244.04164123535156
      ],
      "text": "noted that including bedaquiline in all-oral regimens for children will allow the construction of regimens",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 10.947274208068848,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        242.79859924316406,
        527.41455078125,
        257.2416076660156
      ],
      "text": "that are more child- and family-friendly, with shorter durations (as shown by the IPD analysis, where",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        255.9987335205078,
        527.5848999023438,
        270.4417419433594
      ],
      "text": "bedaquiline-containing regimens were usually shorter than those not including bedaquiline). The",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        269.1986083984375,
        527.4531860351562,
        283.6416320800781
      ],
      "text": "GDG rated the desirable effects as moderate. The main concern noted by the panel was the lack of",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        282.39862060546875,
        527.4408569335938,
        296.8416442871094
      ],
      "text": "data on long-term safety and adverse events. However, the GDG noted that clinical experience with",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        295.5986328125,
        527.3936767578125,
        310.0416564941406
      ],
      "text": "using bedaquiline in young children showed that the drug is tolerated well and often better than in",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        308.798583984375,
        527.4078369140625,
        323.2416076660156
      ],
      "text": "the adult population. Therefore, the GDG agreed that the undesirable effects were small. Overall,",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        321.99859619140625,
        527.433349609375,
        336.4416198730469
      ],
      "text": "the GDG determined that the balance between desirable and undesirable effects probably favours",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        335.1986083984375,
        527.4411010742188,
        349.6416320800781
      ],
      "text": "the use of bedaquiline in children aged below 6 years. The GDG highlighted that the benefits may",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        348.39862060546875,
        527.4389038085938,
        362.8416442871094
      ],
      "text": "vary depending on specific contexts and population characteristics, such as by nutritional status. The",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        361.5986022949219,
        527.4035034179688,
        376.0416259765625
      ],
      "text": "GDG also noted that the potential higher cost of bedaquiline in an MDR/RR-TB treatment regimen",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        374.7986145019531,
        527.5067749023438,
        389.24163818359375
      ],
      "text": "should be considered in the context of the benefits of shorter injectable free regimens (i.e. less travel,",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 10.996500015258789,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        387.99859619140625,
        527.3794555664062,
        402.4416198730469
      ],
      "text": "reduced time spent in clinics and fewer adverse events). In addition, they judged that equity might",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        401.1986083984375,
        527.389404296875,
        415.6416320800781
      ],
      "text": "increase when bedaquiline becomes available to younger children, as its use would be acceptable to",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        414.39862060546875,
        527.6041259765625,
        428.8416442871094
      ],
      "text": "the majority of stakeholders, and that one of the main feasibility aspects would be related to the need",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 10.984689712524414,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        427.5986022949219,
        527.0819702148438,
        442.0416259765625
      ],
      "text": "for safety monitoring (i.e. access to ECG monitoring, as well as staff capacity for monitoring). However,",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 10.975672721862793,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        440.7986145019531,
        524.412353515625,
        455.24163818359375
      ],
      "text": "the panel judged that the use of bedaquiline in young children was probably feasible to implement.",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        465.7812194824219,
        209.15652465820312,
        481.6332092285156
      ],
      "text": "Subgroup considerations",
      "font": "SegoeUI-BoldItalic",
      "size": 12.0,
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        488.66522216796875,
        527.4241943359375,
        503.28424072265625
      ],
      "text": "Children living with HIV:  While trial TMC207-C211 has not yet enrolled children living with HIV, the",
      "font": "SegoeUI-SemiboldItalic",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        502.0411376953125,
        527.4888305664062,
        516.484130859375
      ],
      "text": "IMPAACT study P1108 study enrols HIV-infected and HIV-uninfected infants, children and adolescents",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 10.972565650939941,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        515.2410888671875,
        527.4574584960938,
        529.68408203125
      ],
      "text": "with MDR-TB disease (of the nine children aged below 6 years enrolled and with PK data at the time",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        528.4411010742188,
        527.3726806640625,
        542.8840942382812
      ],
      "text": "of the GDG report, one was HIV-infected). In the paediatric IPD, 12 of the 40 children (30%) aged",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        541.64111328125,
        527.438720703125,
        556.0841064453125
      ],
      "text": "below 6 years treated with a bedaquiline-containing regimen were HIV positive, as compared to 364",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        554.8411865234375,
        413.1631164550781,
        569.2841796875
      ],
      "text": "out of 1992 (20%) treated with DR-TB regimens not including bedaquiline.",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        576.5451049804688,
        527.1403198242188,
        590.9880981445312
      ],
      "text": "The composition of treatment regimens for MDR/RR-TB does not usually differ substantially for people",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 10.962586402893066,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        589.7451171875,
        527.3881225585938,
        604.1881103515625
      ],
      "text": "living with HIV; bedaquiline may be used in all children, irrespective of HIV status. Known drug-drug",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        602.945068359375,
        424.428466796875,
        617.3880615234375
      ],
      "text": "interactions, such as between bedaquiline and efavirenz, need to be avoided.",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        624.4730224609375,
        527.4150390625,
        639.0919799804688
      ],
      "text": "Extrapulmonary TB:  The shorter, all oral bedaquiline-containing regimen is contraindicated in",
      "font": "SegoeUI-SemiboldItalic",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        637.8489990234375,
        527.5606689453125,
        652.2919921875
      ],
      "text": "children with extrapulmonary forms of TB other than TB lymphadenopathy (see implementation",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        651.0490112304688,
        527.4058227539062,
        665.4920043945312
      ],
      "text": "considerations for the full eligibility criteria). Children with these forms of EPTB should be treated",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        661.4550170898438,
        527.4111328125,
        678.6920166015625
      ],
      "text": "(9) with longer regimens, composed of medicines from groups A, B and C  . Data on the penetration",
      "font": "SegoeUI-LightItalic",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        677.448974609375,
        331.8302001953125,
        691.8919677734375
      ],
      "text": "of bedaquiline across the blood-brain barrier are sparse.",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        702.4315795898438,
        245.23455810546875,
        718.2836303710938
      ],
      "text": "Implementation considerations",
      "font": "SegoeUI-BoldItalic",
      "size": 12.0,
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        725.3155517578125,
        527.4267578125,
        739.9345092773438
      ],
      "text": "Eligibility for the shorter, all-oral, bedaquiline containing regimen:  The removal of the age",
      "font": "SegoeUI-SemiboldItalic",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        738.6915283203125,
        527.4376220703125,
        753.134521484375
      ],
      "text": "restriction for the use of bedaquiline means that children of all ages with confirmed MDR/RR-TB and",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        751.8914794921875,
        527.2177734375,
        766.33447265625
      ],
      "text": "without fluoroquinolone resistance may be offered the shorter, all-oral regimen with bedaquiline,",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
